    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antisthĕnes</span></b> , is and ae,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀντισθένης</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a pupil of
				Socrates</i>, <i>teacher of Diogenes</i>, <i>and founder of the Cynic philosophy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antisthenes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 13, 32</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. de Or. 3, 17, 62</span></i>.—In
				plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antisthenae multi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 14, 1, 29</span></i>
			.</div>
